      "content": "Example: Iterator Over a String"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Consider this example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "content": "1name = \"Eva\"\n2\n3for character in name: \n4    print(\"Hello\")"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Here's how you read this for loop code in plain English:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "For each character in the name string, execute the block of code (in this case, printing \"Hello\")."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Output"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "content": "Hello\nHello\nHello"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Since the string has three characters, the loop runs three times, and \"Hello\" is printed once for each character."
    },
